<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philippe Pétain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1856–1951</span> · Also known as Marshal Pétain</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philippe Pétain was a French general and marshal, celebrated as the defender of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/verdun">Verdun</a> in 1916. In June 1940, as prime minister, he sought an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, and on 10 July parliament gave him full powers; as head of the French State at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vichy">Vichy</a> he pursued collaboration and an authoritarian National Revolution. Tried after the Liberation, he was sentenced to death for treason, commuted to life imprisonment, and died on the Île d'Yeu.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philippe-petain.jpg" alt="Philippe Pétain" width="320" height="437" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Imprimerie Draeger à Montrouge en région parisienne · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:P%C3%A9tain_-_portrait_photographique.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
